==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*südän}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*śüdäme}}. Cognate with {{cog|et|süda}}, {{cog|mns|сым}} and {{cog|hu|szív}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fi-IPA}}
* ''Note:'' usually pronounced with a long ''m'' in inflections and derivations (e.g., sydämen [ˈsydæmːen]).

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[heart]]
# [[core]]
#: {{l|fi|reaktorisydän|reaktori'''sydän'''|t=nuclear reactor core, reactor core}}
#: {{syn|fi|ydin}}
# [[wick]] (of a candle)

